# Simplicity First

Optimize for simplicity by default.

- Choose the simplest design that can meet the current requirement.
- Avoid introducing new services, layers, abstractions, or dependencies unless they are necessary to deliver the target feature, safety, or reliability requirement.
- Prefer incremental evolution of existing components over large rewrites.
- When a more complex approach is proposed, explicitly justify why simpler alternatives are insufficient.
- Keep architecture and implementation explanations concise and practical.

When tradeoffs exist, recommend the low-complexity option first and escalate complexity only with clear necessity.
